Vendored zlib (deflate only)

Upstream:  zlib 1.3.1, https://zlib.net/ (Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler)
Source:    https://github.com/madler/zlib/releases/download/v1.3.1/zlib-1.3.1.tar.gz
SHA-256:   9a93b2b7dfdac77ceba5a558a580e74667dd6fede4585b91eefb60f03b72df23
License:   zlib License, see LICENSE (copied from the tarball) and README.

Files copied unmodified from the tarball: adler32.c crc32.c crc32.h deflate.c
deflate.h gzguts.h trees.c trees.h zconf.h zlib.h zutil.c zutil.h LICENSE README.

Why: delta APK patches are generated by a JVM on stock zlib. Rebuilding the
target APK requires recompressing every entry byte-for-byte the same way, and
Android 12+ ships Chromium's zlib fork, whose deflate output differs. The SDK
therefore compresses with this copy (../hands_zlib_deflater.c), built with
Z_PREFIX and hidden visibility so it never clashes with the system libz.

To update: replace these files from a verified release tarball, then recompute
the constants in DeflaterSelfCheck.kt (they must not change for a stock zlib).
